# Copy to .env at the repo root. Git-ignored (.gitignore:193) -- keep it that way,
# this is a checkout of an open-source tree.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# experiments/env.sh reads it on the host and --export=ALL carries the values into
# the container ($HOME is not mounted, so this is the only path in). Anything
# already set in the environment wins, so a single key can be overridden per run
# without editing this file.

# --- Weights & Biases --------------------------------------------------------
# env.sh also falls back to an api.wandb.ai entry in ~/.netrc if this is unset.
WANDB_API_KEY=

# --- HuggingFace -------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed for gated repos; everything else in setup/datasets.txt is public.
# Currently that is Idavidrein/gpqa, which is gated "auto": accepting the terms
# grants access immediately, but the *download* still has to authenticate as the
# account that accepted them.
#
#   1. https://huggingface.co/datasets/Idavidrein/gpqa -> agree to the terms
#   2. https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens -> a read token
#
# Without it `hf download` exits 0 having fetched only the public README, which is
# why download_dataset.sbatch checks for data files rather than the exit status.
HF_TOKEN=

# --- NVIDIA Inference Hub ----------------------------------------------------
# Used by the tau-bench recipe for its user simulator. Mint a key at
#   https://inference.nvidia.com/key-management
# and pick the model(s) there: keys are scoped, and an unscoped one answers
# `key_model_access_denied` for everything except 'default-models'.
#
# On a Regulated (ECCN) tenant the portal offers only Prod keys. That is the
# tenant's design rather than a permissions problem, and Prod is the key type
# this workload wants anyway -- it may use 80% of a model's capacity before rate
# limiting, against 20% for personal/non-prod keys.
NVIDIA_INFERENCE_API_KEY=
# Override only if the endpoint moves.
# NVIDIA_INFERENCE_BASE_URL=https://inference-api.nvidia.com/v1

# The user-simulator model, exactly as its Inference Hub model card names it.
# Required: the recipe refuses to start without it rather than defaulting to a
# model the key may not be scoped to. It needs to be cheap and fast, not clever.
TAU_USER_MODEL=

# Any other litellm provider works instead; set the provider and its own key.
#   TAU_USER_MODEL_PROVIDER=gemini
#   GEMINI_API_KEY=
